<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Disney said cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Disney said cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney analyst Jill Krutick reduced the rating on Walt Disney Co to outperform from buy, according to a Smith Barney source.</p>
<p>-- shares dropped 2-1/2 to 80-3/8.  </p>
<p>-- Krutick said in a research note that the downgrade &quot;is based strictly on valuation relative to earnings growth.&quot;</p>
<p>-- shaved the earnings estimate to $2.75 per share from $2.80 for 1997, and to $3.15 from $3.20 for 1998.</p>
<p>-- said recent spate of investments &quot;could raise corporate expenses and net interest expenses.&quot;</p>
<p>-- set a new price target &quot;into the low $90s.&quot;</p>
</text>
